<title>AUSTRALIA: Central Equity boosts year net profit.</title>
<headline>Central Equity boosts year net profit.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		   22.31  vs  15.27</p>
<p>    Net				    14.27  vs  10.10</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)	    7.0   vs   5.0</p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)	   11.0   vs   9.0</p>
<p>    Sales				 142.60  vs 135.36</p>
<p>    Other income			  4.82  vs   4.57</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			  18.0   vs  13.0</p>
<p>    Abnormal items			nil   vs   nil</p>
<p>Dividend is fully franked  </p>
<p>Pay date Sep 30</p>
<p>Reg date Sep 23</p>
<p>    Tax				     8.05  vs   5.16</p>
<p>    Interest				7.25  vs   2.33</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  0.47  vs   0.40</p>
<p>    Minorities			    nil   vs   nil</p>
<p>NOTE: Central Equity Ltd is a Victorian-based property developer.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 373 1800</p>
</text>
